        "code": {
          "text": "Visual acuity with glasses, without contact lenses"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Right: 6/6. Left: 6/12, improving with pinhole to approximately 6/9−."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Current left-eye symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Eye pain markedly decreased; mild gritty sensation remains. Photophobia improved but persists outdoors. Left vision is slightly blurred but better than before."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated ocular symptoms and history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "At onset approximately 5 days ago, sudden left-eye pain, redness, photophobia, and watery discharge. Today: no headache, nausea, vomiting, flashes, floaters, or curtain over vision. No previous corneal ulcers, known ocular surface disease, or trauma."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "External eye examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild left blepharospasm and occasional left squint in bright light. No periorbital swelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Conjunctival examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Moderate left ciliary and conjunctival injection; right eye within normal limits."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Corneal and anterior chamber examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pen-torch examination shows a small central-paracentral whitish left corneal opacity, approximately 1–2 mm, consistent with the known ulcer. No gross corneal haze or obvious perforation. Anterior chamber appears deep; no obvious hypopyon on torch examination."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Pupils and extraocular movements"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pupils equal, round, and reactive to light; no relative afferent pupillary defect. Extraocular movements intact; no diplopia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
